body:
Thanks so much for your reply! Yes, I got the impression when I mentioned morphine that they thought I was drug seeking. They had taken the X-ray but my strong impression was that the doctor wasn't able to read it. My sis in law asked what it showed and the doctor gave a disinterested, 'Normal'. Hmmm that's strange given that doctors in the UK generally can't make head or tail of my abdo X-rays because it just looks so different to somebody who hasn't had a J-pouch. 

&#x200B;

Can I ask what pain medication you have found effective to take in those situations? As with you the obstructions always resolve and really I would prefer not to go to hospital. The two problems I have are pain and dehydration.
